# the version is named here too: the shlibs come from the library that is installed when this is built
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         librustls-quic0.15.7 (>= 0.15.7+quic3),
Description: ngtcp2 crypto helper for Rustls
 ngtcp2 is an implementation of the QUIC protocol, and leaves the TLS part to
 a library. This is the helper that lets it use Rustls, through
 rustls-ffi-quic (librustls-quic): it hands the handshake bytes to Rustls and
 installs the keys that the traffic secrets of Rustls give. The packet
 protection (AEAD, HKDF, header protection) is done with OpenSSL's libcrypto.
 .
 curl uses it for HTTP/3 over Rustls.

Package: libngtcp2-crypto-rustls-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
